@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] back-today-finds-are-under-leaves
A find in Back today that has not been opened MUST lie under fallen leaves that hide it
whole, its words hidden from accessibility too, laid out the same each time for the same
card. A tap MUST blow the leaves away from where the finger landed, the nearest first,
lifting, turning and fading past the tile's edges, and MUST open the find while they
are still flying. The find then counts as visited: its star lights (`visit`, sent
through the outbox so it waits offline like any change, gallery-keeps-offline-changes)
and it shows uncovered for the rest of the day. An opened find MUST NOT be covered again
that day. The leaves MUST NOT move while untouched, so the band costs nothing while the
gallery scrolls.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026, 23:06 ("do the new stuff you mentioned for the Worn
stuff"); the leaves are Claude's pick, 11 Leaves of the 30 worn directions on the
"Your sky" canvas, not yet confirmed by Tavi.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] sky-opens-from-the-star-button
On All, a star button MUST sit beside Add once the sky has anything to show: a
constellation forming or finished, or a find opened again. Before that it MUST NOT
show, so it never opens an empty sky. When a find in Back today is uncovered, a star
MUST fly from where the finger lifted the leaves to the star button and the button
glows as it lands, before the find has opened over it. The button opens Your sky over
the gallery: the tab bar steps away as it does for reels, and Back or Close shuts it.
A find opened from the sky rises over it, and closing the find returns to the sky.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026, 23:06 ("implement all this other stuff into the actual
app"), building the "Your sky" prototype into the app. The button's place beside Add
and the star's flight are Claude's choices, not yet confirmed by Tavi.

