Your sky MUST show these, over a still nebula:
- The active constellation, large. Its stars are lit for finds opened again since it
  formed and dark otherwise, with gold lines between lit stars and dotted lines to dark
  ones.
- The finished constellations, smaller, with their figures drawn in.
- Loose stars for the other finds opened from Back today.
Its only words MUST be its title and the active constellation's name. No hints,
sentences, counts, quests or levels go on the sky. A constellation MUST be drawn as one
of the line figures, one for each figure the server names, and never with a find's
words. Each star MUST name its find to accessibility. Tapping a star opens its find,
which counts as a visit. Stars MAY twinkle only while the sky shows, and the nebula is
painted once.
Source: Tavi's reviews of the "Your sky" prototype, 5 November 2026:
